[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/pulls/203","id":3950369965,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQJkZtc7rddyt","html_url":"https://github.com/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/pull/203","diff_url":"https://github.com/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/pull/203.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/pull/203.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/issues/203","number":203,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"V1.7.0","user":{"login":"Leg0shii","id":46093332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDkzMzMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46093332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii","html_url":"https://github.com/Leg0shii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## v1.7.0\n\n### Highlights\n- **Minecraft 26.2 support**: the Fabric loader now runs on the latest Minecraft (updated from 1.21.10). (#161)\n- **Free start position**: the Angle Solver can now treat the starting position as part of the solve. Instead of manually nudging the start and re-solving, the solver picks the best spot within the start block's footprint for you. (#216, closes #113, #195)\n- **Angle Solver node editor**: build solver pipelines as a node graph, with per-stage budget controls in Custom effort. (#228, closes #217, #221)\n- **Client-sided multiplayer playback**: watch a TAS replay run its route while you're on a server, on all three loaders. Fully client-sided: only you can see the replay, your own player never moves, and nothing is sent to the server. Input playback that moves your player in multiplayer remains disabled on purpose.\n\n### Angle Solver\n- New constraint types:\n  - **Relative X/Z**: give an X or Z constraint a reference tick and it constrains the offset from that tick instead of an absolute coordinate.\n  - **Per-tick deltas dX, dZ, dF**: constrain how far a tick moves or turns compared to the previous tick, with fast closed-form solving for dF.\n  - **dX vs dZ** comparison mode on dX, for constraining which axis moves more.\n- **Constraint hotkeys**: press **B** to add wall/footprint constraints for the block you're looking at, **Ctrl+B** for ladder, slime, and ice cell constraints. (#208)\n- Tight jumps that used to come up just short now land: Optimize and Custom effort run a budgeted rescue search when the solver gets very close to feasible.\n- More reliable solving overall: improved path recovery when the fast solve stage fails. (#209, closes #204)\n- Fast effort now stops as soon as it finds a working solution instead of burning the full time budget. (#201)\n\n### Visualization & controls\n- **Hit distance lines**: per-tick lines showing your 4.5-block reach, so you can see which blocks are hittable on each tick.\n- **Pitch gizmo**: Ctrl + right-drag now adjusts pitch, and the facing arrow can show the full look direction (yaw + pitch).\n- **Block capture (experimental)**: pick real blocks from the world, including their exact collision shapes, on all three loaders. Enable it in Settings.\n\n### Simulation accuracy\n- Fixed cobweb desync between the simulated path and the real game. (#200)\n- Fixed sprint acceleration being applied one tick early; the simulation now matches Minecraft's delayed sprint factor exactly. (#207)\n\n### Performance\n- Editing inputs on very long TASes no longer causes lag spikes: the rendered path is now patched in place instead of fully rebuilt on every change.\n\n### Fixes\n- Fixed startup crash on Apple Silicon Macs. (#206, closes #205)\n- \"Save as...\" is now disabled when no TAS is open. (#231, closes #158)\n- Clicking a tick in the input table now jumps to the correct position.\n- Constraint hotkeys now use their own raycast, so they target the block you're actually looking at.\n- Relative pitch turns now allow up to 180 degrees.\n- Released jars no longer contain process-spawning bytecode from bundled libraries, so they pass Modrinth's automated review.\n","created_at":"2026-06-28T09:20:26Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T12:02:16Z","closed_at":"2026-07-26T08:11:08Z","merged_at":"2026-07-26T08:11:08Z","merge_commit_sha":"75cff6dd0c3ace69e78645f7c3a324cad8e2e469","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/pulls/203/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/pulls/203/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/issues/203/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leg0shii/ParkourCalculatorMod/statuses/d3593abc94c3c00e1e1c505ba51552f17f76c921","head":{"label":"Leg0shii:v1.7.0","ref":"v1.7.0","sha":"d3593abc94c3c00e1e1c505ba51552f17f76c921","user":{"login":"Leg0shii","id":46093332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDkzMzMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46093332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii","html_url":"https://github.com/Leg0shii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leg0shii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/